            <ArticleTitle>Acute myeloid leukemia presenting as splenic rupture.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1435-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a rare case of acute myeloid leukemia presenting primarily as an acute abdomen due to spontaneous splenic rupture in a 19 years male patient. He was treated with splenectomy after failure of conservative management for splenic preservation but later succumbed to an intracerebral haemorrhage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
